## Recipe Box
// Your recipes, on cards:  find one, add one, change one as you type, remove one and undo it.
// Where they're kept is the next line, and only that line knows.  Change it to keep them somewhere else:
//   family cookbook is a folder at "http://127.0.0.1:4791/api/places/recipes"
//   family cookbook is a live room at "http://127.0.0.1:4791/api/rooms/recipes"
// (Both are served on your computer by "yarn tsx scripts/recipe-servers.ts", at the top of Spell's folder.)
family cookbook is this device


## A recipe:  a card you can read and change
a "recipe" is a view:
	- it is saved in the family cookbook
	- its "title" is text
	- its "servings" is a number
	- its "notes" is text
	- to draw it:
		<ui-card fluid>
			<ui-content>
				<ui-form value={it} class="recipe">
					<ui-field label="Recipe name">
						<ui-input name="title" class="title" size="large"/>
					</ui-field>
					<ui-field label="Serves" inline>
						<ui-input class="serves" name="servings" type="number" min="1" labeled="right" label="people"/>
					</ui-field>
					<ui-field label="Notes">
						<ui-textarea name="notes" rows="2" grow/>
					</ui-field>
				</ui-form>
			</ui-content>
			<ui-extra part="foot">
				<ui-button class="remove" size="small" appearance="basic" onClick={remove it from the recipes}>Remove</ui-button>
			</ui-extra>
		</ui-card>


## The box:  the card for a new recipe, then a card for each one you have
recipe box is an app:
	- its "search" is text
	- its "new recipe" is a new recipe with servings = 4
	- its "matches" is every recipe where its title includes the search
	- its "box menu" is a menu of "undo"

	// With nothing kept yet, a few to start from
	- to create it:
		if the number of (every recipe) is 0
			add (a new recipe with title = "Tomato soup", servings = 4, notes = "Roast the tomatoes first.") to the recipes
			add (a new recipe with title = "Dal", servings = 6, notes = "Add the spices last.") to the recipes
			add (a new recipe with title = "Pizza Margherita", servings = 2, notes = "A very hot oven.") to the recipes

	- to add the new recipe:
		add its new recipe to the recipes
		set its new recipe to a new recipe with servings = 4

	- to draw it:
		<header class="top">
			<div class="heading">
				<h1>Recipe Box</h1>
				<p>Everything you type is saved as you go.</p>
			</div>
			<ui-toolbar class="undo" menu="box menu" aria-label="Recipes"/>
			<ui-form value={it}>
				<ui-field label="Search">
					<ui-input name="search" class="search" icon="search"/>
				</ui-field>
			</ui-form>
		</header>
		<ui-card fluid class="new">
			<ui-content>
				<ui-form value={its new recipe}>
					<h2>Add a recipe</h2>
					<ui-field label="Recipe name">
						<ui-input name="title" class="draft" size="large"/>
					</ui-field>
					<ui-field label="Serves" inline>
						<ui-input class="serves" name="servings" type="number" min="1" labeled="right" label="people"/>
					</ui-field>
					<ui-field label="Notes">
						<ui-textarea name="notes" rows="2" grow/>
					</ui-field>
				</ui-form>
			</ui-content>
			<ui-extra>
				<ui-button class="add" size="small" color="primary" disabled={the title of its new recipe is ""} onClick={add the new recipe}>Add recipe</ui-button>
			</ui-extra>
		</ui-card>
		for each recipe in the matches
			draw the recipe
		while waiting:
			<ui-loader class="waiting" visible inline text>Finding your recipes</ui-loader>
		if there are none:
			<ui-text class="none">{"No recipes yet. Add your first one." if the search is "" otherwise "No recipes match your search."}</ui-text>
		if that fails:
			<ui-message class="failed" color="red">
				<p>We can't reach your recipes right now.</p>
				<ui-button class="again" onClick={try again}>Try again</ui-button>
			</ui-message>


start the recipe box
